    <string name="about_safety_title">Safety</string>
    <string name="about_safety">Car Reader reads diagnostic data. It does no remapping or tuning, and never changes emission systems, the odometer or the immobilizer. The only change it can make is clearing fault codes, which is off by default and always needs safety checks and your confirmation.</string>
    <string name="about_sources_title">Data sources</string>
    <string name="about_sources">Standard OBD-II definitions follow SAE J1979 and SAE J2012. Brand-specific signal definitions come from the OBDb project (https://github.com/OBDb). Control module addresses are community-sourced.</string>
    <string name="about_licenses_title">Licenses</string>
    <string name="about_licenses">OBDb vehicle signal data © OBDb contributors, source https://github.com/OBDb, licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/. Adapted: Mode 22 signals selected and converted. Libraries: Kotlin, kotlinx.coroutines, kotlinx.serialization, AndroidX and Jetpack Compose (Apache License 2.0).</string>
